					<description><![CDATA[<p style="font-style: italic;">The latest advisory follows earlier notices issued in 2023, 2025 and 2026 identifying multiple fake Supreme Court websites.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.scconline.com/blog/post/2026/11/03/supreme-court-warns-fake-websites-phishing-scam-scigovinjudicial/">Fake Supreme Court website alert: SC flags &#8220;scigovinjudicial.com&#8221; as phishing domain</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.scconline.com/blog">SCC Times</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<div style="text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;">
<p style="margin-bottom: 3%;">The Supreme Court of India has issued another public advisory cautioning the public against fraudulent websites impersonating its official online presence. In a notice dated <span style="font-weight: bold;">3 November 2026</span>, the Supreme Court Registry identified &#8220;<span style="font-weight: bold;">scigovinjudicial.com</span>&#8221; as a newly detected fraudulent domain that may be used to obtain sensitive personal information and confidential credentials through phishing.</p> ]]></content:encoded>
					
