<item>
		<title>Quackery and right to health under Article 21: Allahabad High Court issues notice on PIL seeking AI-based doctor verification and stricter regulation of clinical establishments</title>
		<link>https://www.scconline.com/blog/post/2026/11/03/allahabad-hc-pil-seeks-ban-on-quacks-unlicensed-clinical-establishments/</link>
					<comments>https://www.scconline.com/blog/post/2026/11/03/allahabad-hc-pil-seeks-ban-on-quacks-unlicensed-clinical-establishments/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Ankita Kumari]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 12:00:54 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Case Briefs]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[High Courts]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AI-based verification of doctors]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Allahabad High Court]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Clinical Establishments Act 2010]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Cross-disciplinary medical practice]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Digital medical registers]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[IGRS/Jansunwai grievance redressal]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Inter-departmental task force]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[National Commission for Indian System of Medicine Act 2020]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[National Medical Commission Act 2019]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[pil]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Prevention of unauthorised medical practice]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Protection against quackery]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[public interest litigation]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Regulation of clinical establishments]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Right to Health under Article 21]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[State Council of Clinical Establishments]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Unlicensed clinical establishments]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Unqualified medical practitioners]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[uttar pradesh]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.scconline.com/blog/?p=400438</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p style="font-style: italic;">The PIL calls for an effective roadmap to eliminate quackery, prevent cross-disciplinary medical practice by unqualified persons and ensure that only duly qualified practitioners operate clinical establishments</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.scconline.com/blog/post/2026/11/03/allahabad-hc-pil-seeks-ban-on-quacks-unlicensed-clinical-establishments/">Quackery and right to health under Article 21: Allahabad High Court issues notice on PIL seeking AI-based doctor verification and stricter regulation of clinical establishments</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.scconline.com/blog">SCC Times</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<div style="text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;">
<p style="margin-bottom: 3%;"><span style="font-weight: bold;">Allahabad High Court:</span> While considering a Public Interest Litigation (PIL) on quackery and right to life and health under Article <a href="https://www.scconline.com/DocumentLink.aspx?q=JTXT-0001574949" target="_blank">21</a> of the <a href="https://www.scconline.com/DocumentLink.aspx?q=JTXT-0002726967" target="_blank">Constitution</a>, seeking recognition of the right to protection from quacks and unqualified medical practitioners, and prohibition on the operation of unlicensed clinical establishments, as an integral component of the Right to Life and Health under Article <a href="https://www.scconline.com/DocumentLink.aspx?q=JTXT-0001574949" target="_blank">21</a> of the <a href="https://www.scconline.com/DocumentLink.aspx?q=JTXT-0002726967" target="_blank">Constitution</a>, the Division Bench of Rajan Roy and Manjive Shukla, JJ., issued notice to the respondents and directed that the matter be connected with a pending PIL raising overlapping issues.</p> ]]></content:encoded>
					
